From 44fafbc6621287ee0211e87d45a7ba0aa00d3718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:22:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [FOR-UPSTREAM] platform/x86: msi-wmi-platform: terminate
 msi_quirks DMI table

The msi_quirks table lacks a terminating empty entry so it crashes the
kernel on non-quirked MSI Claw devices.

Fixes: bfd56a3d6de5 ("[FROM-ML] platform/x86: msi-wmi-platform: Add quirk system")
Signed-off-by: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Henry Paradiz <henry.paradiz@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/msi-wmi-platform.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/msi-wmi-platform.c b/drivers/platform/x86/msi-wmi-platform.c
index 11ac3fb7dc62..6a19e0c45de2 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/msi-wmi-platform.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/msi-wmi-platform.c
@@ -282,6 +282,7 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id msi_quirks[] = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = &quirk_gen3,
 	},
+	{ }
 };
 
 static int msi_wmi_platform_parse_buffer(union acpi_object *obj, u8 *output, size_t length)
-- 
2.55.0

